A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ defined by:

$$
f(x) = \begin{cases}
    ax & \text{for } 0 \le x \le k \\
    0 & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}
$$


where $a$ and $k$ are positive constants.

Given that the variance of $X$ is 2, what is the value of $k$?
